					</actions>
				</button>
				<text_box x="11" y="15" width="1033" height="77">The susceptible-infected-recovered (SIR) model with losing immunity simulates the Suceptible, Infected, and Recovered population during an infectious outbreak. Click [Run simulation] to generate a new synthetic data set from a randomly selected uniform distribution of Contact Rate, Infectivity, Total Population, and Average Length of Immunity. See the observed variables for the latent Susceptible, Infected, and Recovered population. Click [Export observed vars] to download a .csv file in wide format of the simulated data. Click [Export latent vars] to download a .csv file in wide format of the simulated latent variables, which you can use to compare results from estimating values using continuous SEM against the simulated system. Click [Clear results] to clear the graph.</text_box>
				<numeric_input label_side="left" wrap_title="true" input_width="50" x="90.5" y="477.5" width="94" height="39" min="0" max="50" isee:navigate_to="false" show_name="true">
